cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this book in your teaching or research, please cite it as below.
title: 'Accounting Analytics: An Integrated Approach'
abstract: 'Accounting Analytics: An Integrated Approach is an open textbook that teaches accounting and business
  students to extract, prepare, analyze, and visualize financial and operational data with Microsoft Excel, SQL,
  and Microsoft Power BI. Every technique is taught through an accounting question, and every example draws on the
  records of one fictional company in the Charles River Accounting Dataset, so a customer order analyzed in Excel
  is the same one found in the general ledger with SQL and reported on in Power BI. Part I lays the foundations
  of accounting analytics, data quality, and the relational database behind accounting systems. Part II teaches
  data preparation, descriptive analytics, forecasting, budgeting, what-if analysis, and audit testing in Excel.
  Part III queries, joins, and summarizes whole populations of transactions in SQL, for management questions and
  for audit tests. Part IV turns to data visualization, data models, DAX measures, management reports, and audit
  monitoring in Power BI. Part V offers capstone cases in financial reporting, managerial accounting, and auditing.
  The chapters of Parts I to IV combine guided tutorials, multiple-choice questions, and exercises from the perspectives
  of financial accounting, managerial accounting, and auditing, and each of these Parts closes with a comprehensive
  case. The book is written for undergraduate and graduate students with no prior analytics or programming experience.
  It is free to read online and to download, as are its dataset, slides, companion files, and solutions, and it
  is licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0.'
